cmake bootstrap: leave the GHS generator header out

The bootstrap never registers cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator (its factory is
behind !CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP) and does not build its source, but cmake.cxx
still includes the header, whose inline NewFactory() instantiates the
factory template. Built with GCC 16 at -O2, cmake::CreateGlobalGenerator
then refers to the generator directly and the bootstrap fails to link:
undefined reference to cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator(cmake*) and
GetDocumentation(). Include the header only where it is used.

--- a/Source/cmake.cxx	2024-08-29 16:37:11.000000000 -0300
+++ b/Source/cmake.cxx	2026-11-18 12:54:09.675937437 -0300
@@ -130,7 +130,8 @@
 
 // NOTE: the __linux__ macro is predefined on Android host too, but
 // main CMakeLists.txt filters out this generator by host name.
-#if (defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)) || defined(_WIN32)
+#if !defined(CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP) && \
+  ((defined(__linux__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)) || defined(_WIN32))
 #  include "cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.h"
 #endif
 
